<title>USA: Armstrong offers C$23/shr for Domco.</title>
<headline>Armstrong offers C$23/shr for Domco.</headline>
<dateline>LANCASTER, Pa. 1997-06-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>Floor and wall covering maker Armstrong World Industries Inc said Monday it had offered to buy its Canadian rival, Domco Inc, for C$488 million.</p>
<p>The offer includes C$23 per Domco share, plus bids for Domco's convertible debtentures, warrants and other convertible securities, Lancaster, Pa.-based Armstrong said.</p>
<p>The offer represents a 56.0 percent premium over Domco's closing share price Friday of C$14.75, said Armstrong.</p>
<p>Armstrong, whose shares closed Friday at 68-5/8, said it made the offer in a letter sent to Domco and Domco's majority shareholder, Sommer Allibert.</p>
<p>Officials from Domco were not available for comment.</p>
</text>
